     3,
     "<div><div name=\"messageReplySection\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">On 4 Sep 2020, 02:52 +0300, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">annaka...@gmail.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">annaka...@gmail.com</a>&gt;, wrote:</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">Hi!</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">I&#39;m very new to both Bayesian analysis and INLA, and am trying to learn both by working through the Statistical Rethinking book homework that use the rethinking package (which is STAN-based) using INLA.</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">I&#39;m trying to replicate the results from a mixed effects model with correlated random effects for the slope and intercept. While I am able to replicate the summary estimates of the fixed effects and hyperparameters, I don&#39;t obtain the same individual estimates for the random effect. I think it&#39;s because I&#39;m unsure of how to extract the second vector of the correlated random effect that is copied for the slope random effect (see code below). My plots from the INLA model aren&#39;t on the same scale as those from the rethinking model. </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">Any help would be appreciated! </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"> • this is the code using rethinking: <a href=\"https://github.com/rmcelreath/statrethinking_winter2019/blob/master/homework/week09_solutions.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rmcelreath/statrethinking_winter2019/blob/master/homework/week09_solutions.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440433910000&amp;usg=AOvVaw36TFQMrzMld4f-xOG8736a\">https://github.com/rmcelreath/statrethinking_winter2019/blob/master/homework/week09_solutions.pdf</a></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">### HW9.1 in rethinking </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">library(rethinking) </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">data(bangladesh)</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">d &lt;- bangladesh</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">dat_list &lt;- list(</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">  C = d$use.contraception,</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">  did = as.integer( as.factor(d$district) ), </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">  urban = d$urban</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">)</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">m1.1 &lt;- ulam( </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">  alist(</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    C ~ bernoulli( p ),</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    logit(p) &lt;- a[did] + b[did]*urban,</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    c(a,b)[did] ~ multi_normal( c(abar,bbar) , Rho , Sigma ), </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    abar ~ normal(0,1),</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    bbar ~ normal(0,0.5),</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    Rho ~ lkj_corr(2),</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">    Sigma ~ exponential(1) </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">  ) , data=dat_list , chains=4 , cores=4 )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">precis(m1.1)</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">precis( m1.1 , depth=3 , pars=c(&quot;Rho&quot;,&quot;Sigma&quot;) )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">## plot individual effects in rethinking</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">post &lt;- extract.samples(m1.1)</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">a &lt;- apply( post$a , 2 , mean ) </blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">b &lt;- apply( post$b , 2 , mean )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">plot( a, b , xlab=&quot;a (intercept)&quot; , ylab=&quot;b (urban slope)&quot; )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">abline( h=0 , lty=2 )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">abline( v=0 , lty=2 )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">## plot in the outcome scale in rethinking</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\"><br></blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">u0 &lt;- inv_logit( a )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">u1 &lt;- inv_logit( a + b )</blockquote>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border-left-color:rgb(26,188,156);margin:0px;padding-left:10px;border-left-width:thin;border-left-style:solid;padding-bottom:5px;padding-top:5px\">plot( u0 , u1 , xlim=c(0,1) , ylim=c(0,1) , xlab=&quot;urban = 0&quot; , ylab=&quot;urba